# No environment variables are required.
#
# The build runs, all three missions play end to end, and the result measures,
# scores and navigates with nothing configured. That is a requirement of the
# brief rather than an accident (§6 — the experience must be deterministic and
# must not depend on APIs or network timing), so keep it that way: a demo whose
# core loop needs a key is a demo that dies on stage.
#
# This file is committed while .env* is gitignored, so a fresh clone can read it
# and confirm it needs to configure nothing. Do not add a filled-in value here.
